{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When I would heal</b> — Because he said: כי הוא טרף וירפאנו (for he tore us and he healed us), he says: when I wish to heal them, [their wickedness is apparent] — they stand before the wicked in their hearts, who have not abandoned Him until now." "<b>For their deed is falsehood</b> — At night they steal, and by day raiding bands [operate] outside the cities."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The first word of the comment, כרפאי, is Ibn Ezra's lemma from the verse; rendered here as the translated lemma head. The clause in brackets does not appear in the Hebrew; the syntax of the second sentence is compressed and the connection between the clauses is not made explicit."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:26.583166790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}